SDD Open began in April 2026 as a customization of AgentSpec 4.2 (then published as
SpecGate v1.0.0, August 2026) and has since diverged substantially. What descends from
AgentSpec is the phase structure of the workflow — the progression from specification
through design to build, and the practice of keeping phase artifacts as versioned
documents in the repository.

The following are additions developed independently and are not part of AgentSpec:

  - The Verify Gate: acceptance as an executable command, with the six-state exit
    contract (0/2/3/4/5/64), its runner sdd/bin/verify-gate.sh, and the --strict mode
  - The clarification protocol and its dedicated exit state
  - The graded release verdict (PASS / CONCERNS / FAIL / WAIVED) and the waiver taxonomy
  - The evidence contract for build reports (sdd/bin/report-lint.py)
  - The landmine playbook in ACE-lite format (stable IDs, counters, delta-only updates,
    sdd/bin/playbook-lint.sh) — the delta-update idea follows Agentic Context Engineering
    (arXiv:2510.04618)
  - The fresh-context evaluation protocol and the adversarial review contract
  - The agent-agnostic packaging: skills in .agents/skills/ following the Agent Skills
    specification (agentskills.io), the managed block in AGENTS.md (agents.md), and the
    adapter generator bin/sdd-open.sh
  - The EARS requirements grammar integration (the grammar itself is due to
    Alistair Mavin, Rolls-Royce, 2009 — https://alistairmavin.com/ears/)

AgentSpec remains actively maintained by its author as a separate project.
SDD Open is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or a fork of it in the git sense:
this repository was created clean-room, with no shared history.
